--- PARITY with web/src/components/data-display/ProgressRing.tsx ---
Pure-presentational gauge. Full background <circle> track -> native Ellipse; stroke-dash value arc swept value/max
from 12 o'clock -> native rounded-cap arc Path via ChartGeometry.RingArc (full sweep drawn at 0.9999 so a complete
ring never degenerates to a zero-length segment). Optional centred main/sub readout (tabular figures;
main = max(10, round(size*0.32)), sub = max(8, round(size*0.18))) and optional caption beneath. Geometry mirrors the
source exactly: radius = (size-strokeWidth)/2, center = size/2, circumference = 2*PI*r,
clamped = max(0, min(value, max)), dashOffset = circ - frac*circ. The web color hex is replaced by a token-driven
ChartRole / ColorIndex (ADR-009; default index 0 -> TsChart01Brush, the token analogue of the web default #3b82f6)
so the arc stays theme-aware. The ring always renders (track + arc) even at value 0 -> never a blank box. Inputs are
sanitised (non-finite/non-positive size -> default diameter; stroke clamped within the diameter; value clamped and
non-finite -> 0; non-positive max -> empty but drawn ring) so a hostile config never throws or degenerates.
Pure-presentational (no hooks / no network) -> no loading/error/stale/offline chrome; the reproduced render branches
are with/without centred main readout, with/without centred sub readout, and with/without caption, across the
value-clamp range. The source is anonymous (no i18n keys; centre readouts + caption are caller-supplied,
already-localized strings) -> no English literals in native code. The centre overlay is decorative (web aria-hidden);
the composed readout (caption + centre readouts, or a whole-number percent fallback such as "72%") is the surface's
accessible name via a Text automation peer, so Narrator announces the value rather than traversing inner glyphs. No
motion -> inherently reduced-motion-safe; text honours the system text-scale factor. Diagnostics: view.opened
slug=ProgressRing (PII-safe, value never logged).

Native class is Ts-prefixed (TsProgressRing) per the repo convention for native controls that collide with a WinUI
built-in -- here Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls.ProgressRing (the indeterminate spinner used elsewhere in shared-surfaces
via .IsActive). The surface, slug (ProgressRing), automation id (progress-ring) and state holder (ProgressRingViewModel)
are unchanged. No charts/maps used; no atomic-component duplication (reuses ChartGeometry/ChartShapes/ChartBrushes +
DisplayTokens).

